{"id": "EUVD-2026-83618", "enisaUuid": "64e0c5e2-6f3c-3a45-8186-bbe538a5d87f", "description": "Expat before 2.8.5 fails to validate that a high surrogate in UTF-16 input is followed by a low surrogate, allowing malformed UTF-16 sequences to be accepted. Attackers can supply UTF-16 encoded XML containing lone high surrogates that consume the following code unit, causing Expat to pass unpaired surrogates to applications built with XML_UNICODE and to silently replace input characters in other builds.", "datePublished": "2026-09-19T22:58:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-28T16:11:06", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/pull/1282", "https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/commit/ff6e1d7e750bbe245178f51a47a965dc8342861a", "https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/releases/tag/R_2_8_5", "https://blog.hartwork.org/posts/expat-2-8-5-released/", "https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/expat-through-2.8.4-malformed-utf-16-acceptance-via-unchecked-surrogate"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rfp9-ffqc-h4x8", "CVE-2026-93990"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.4, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1383d8cf-0744-35f0-88ba-5b13345a1319", "product": {"name": "libexpat", "vendor": {"name": "libexpat project"}}, "product_version": "0 <2.8.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "edc540d8-8361-320d-9b29-56948b4f85bd", "vendor": {"name": "libexpat"}}], "isExploited": false}